# AutoGuard AI — Cybernetic Tactical HUD Guidelines

## 1. Color Palette Tokens
- **Backgrounds:** `bg-slate-950`, `bg-slate-900/90`, with `backdrop-blur-md` glassmorphism and subtle grid textures.
- **Accents & Telemetry:** Cyan (`text-cyan-400`, `border-cyan-500/30`, `bg-cyan-950/40`), Emerald (`text-emerald-400`, `border-emerald-500/30`), Amber (`text-amber-400`, `border-amber-500/30`), Red Alert (`text-red-400`, `border-red-500/40`, `bg-red-950/30`).
- **Scanlines & Corner Brackets:** Use tactical monospace fonts (`font-mono`) and cyber corner clips (`border-l-2 border-t-2 border-cyan-500`).

## 2. Haptic & Motion Interactions
- Trigger subtle vibration haptic cues via `hapticsService.lightPulse()` on tab switches and metric toggles.
- Trigger double pulse (`hapticsService.warningPulse()`) on safety warnings and triple pulse (`hapticsService.errorAlarm()`) on DTC/critical faults.
- Use `motion/react` or CSS animations for smooth transitions without layout shifts.

## 3. Responsive & Touch Controls
- Minimum touch target size: 44px $\times$ 44px for field tablet ergonomics.
- Ensure all canvas elements handle `devicePixelRatio` and window resize listeners with proper cleanup.
